 nielsS:{n:"Niels (Nils) Stub",st:"prob",line:"olsen",role:"11th great-grandfather (probable) · born abroad",d:"1580",ev:[["1580","Died. Lawman (lagmann) in Oslo and one of the Danish king's central officials in Norway. He came from Denmark and was probably related to Peder Stub, mayor of Viborg",["snlnils","snlstub","lhwstub"]]],note:"Regarded as the founder of this Stub family. He was probably born in Denmark, not England. The intermediate generations here follow the published genealogies of the family."},
 jorgen:{n:"Jørgen (Johan) Daniel Stub",st:"doc",line:"olsen",par:["johanDS"],role:"4th great-grandfather",b:"c. 1782",ev:[["1781","Probably born this year, son of the district judge Johan Daniel Stub (1736–1802)",["lhwstub"]],["1815","Head of the household at Fylling, Borgund, aged 33, with his wife Stine Margrete and sons Christopher, Johan Daniel and Matthias Didrik",["c1815"]],["1824","Merchant (handelsmand)",["k1824b"]],["1839","Named as Kristofer's father",["m1839"]]],note:"Records give his first name as both Jørgen and Johan. He is very probably the Johan Daniel Johansen Stub (1781–1840) of the published Stub genealogy, whose son Matthias Diderik Stub (b. 1814) was a customs officer in Haram and Ålesund. Our 1815 census shows a son Matthias Didrik in his household. That links our Stubs to the old official family descended from Niels Stub (d. 1580), who was probably born in Denmark. This is marked Probable. This Stub line points to Denmark. The name Britanus (Johan J. K. Britanus Stub) is a traditional Sunnmøre given name and does not refer to Britain."},
